  "worked_solution": "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, computing $\\{-2,0,2\\}\\times \\{1,4\\}$ gives the following set:\n\n$$\nS=\\{(-2,1),(-2,4),(0,1),(0,4),(2,1),(2,4)\\}.\n$$\n\nOur visualization of this set is shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14242415/assets/86598866633d3a49c13cf979b0c2c9de74d147e4584a1c6a88847434bc9d3bbf.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
